Chapter: DiagramAliasProbe
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Diagram chapter SelectionManager
  cites Diagram chapter DiagramModel

 Guards the class-F __record-set lift in apps/diagram (BACKLOG 7.16). Each
 nested __record-set chain became a let-chain; a mis-threaded chain still
 compiles but silently drops the earlier writes, leaving a field nobody
 reads unset. This probe exercises lifted chains whose chapters compile
 standalone and asserts every write survives in the final value: the first,
 a middle, and the last write of selection-start-drag (a 5-field chain), and
 the first and last of diagram-add-node and diagram-add-edge. The many chains
 in Diagram.codex and Canvas are inspection-verified (their chapters do not
 yet compile); all are structurally identical same-object threads.

Section: Probe

  check : Boolean, Integer -> Integer
  check (ok) (bit) = if ok then bit else 0

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    let sel = selection-start-drag selection-empty 7 11
    in let a1 = check (sel.sel-dragging == True) 1
    in let a2 = check (sel.sel-drag-y == 11) 2
    in let a3 = check (sel.sel-drag-oy == 11) 4
    in let dg = diagram-add-node (diagram-new "T" Flowchart) ShapeRect 5 6 100 50 "n"
    in let a4 = check (list-length dg.dg-nodes == 1) 8
    in let a5 = check (dg.dg-next-id == 2) 16
    in let dg2 = diagram-add-edge dg 1 1 "e"
    in let a6 = check (list-length dg2.dg-edges == 1) 32
    in let a7 = check (dg2.dg-next-id == 3) 64
    in print-line-uni ("diagram-alias-probe: " & show (a1 + a2 + a3 + a4 + a5 + a6 + a7))
  end
